      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previously I had a bug with the future/promise into the HAL.\nThis is intended to ensure the `Start()` of the module will not return before the `initializationComplete()` callback is called by the HAL.\nThe `TestBackend::initialization_delay`, do a sleep of this amount of time before calling the `initializationComplete()` signal. I check we can observe this sleep (at least 100ms before return of the \"Start()\").\nSo the purpose is to verify that `initialize()` is called, and the function does not return until `initializationComplete()` is called.\nI don\u0027t know how to check that we effectively block on the semaphore (promise/future), without enforcing a very long (100ms) asynchronous acknowledgement.\n\n(This test would fail if you remove the \".wait()\" here: https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Bluetooth/+/3063345/5/system/gd/hal/hci_hal_android.cc#169)",
      "parentUuid": "0db746f3_a0db294a",
      "revId": "59f22d3bdbcd920a06a60c22596d78e4c1615276",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
